== 7.6 Chapter 7 Practice Drill — 40 Questions

40 questions graded in the order the CBT engine is likely to meet them. Allow 44 minutes; the key and a full solution for every question follow.

#mcq(1, [Assets are revalued before a partner is admitted because],
  [the old partners must be credited with gains they have already earned],
  [the new partner must pay for the assets],
  [the law requires an annual valuation],
  [the bank insists on it]
)

#mcq(2, [A profit on revaluation is shared among],
  [the new partners only],
  [the old partners in the old ratio],
  [the partners in the new ratio],
  [all partners including the new one, equally]
)

#mcq(3, [A building is written up from ₦200,000 to ₦260,000 on revaluation. The gain is],
  [₦260,000],
  [₦460,000],
  [₦60,000],
  [₦200,000]
)

#mcq(4, [Stock is written down from ₦80,000 to ₦70,000 on revaluation. This is],
  [a debit to goodwill],
  [a credit in the revaluation account],
  [a credit to capital directly],
  [a debit in the revaluation account]
)

#mcq(5, [Goodwill brought in cash by a new partner is credited to],
  [the revaluation account],
  [the realisation account],
  [the new partner's capital account],
  [the old partners' capital accounts in the old ratio]
)

#mcq(6, [When goodwill is raised in the books and then written off, the write-off is shared],
  [by the new partner alone],
  [equally between the old partners],
  [among all the partners in the new ratio],
  [among the old partners in the old ratio]
)

#mcq(7, [A and B share profits 2:1 with capitals of ₦200,000 and ₦100,000. C is admitted for a one-quarter share, bringing ₦120,000. The total capital of the new firm is],
  [₦400,000],
  [₦420,000],
  [₦450,000],
  [₦300,000]
)

#mcq(8, [Using the last figures, C's share of the capital is],
  [₦120,000],
  [₦140,000],
  [₦100,000],
  [₦105,000]
)

#mcq(9, [A retiring partner is entitled to],
  [the whole of the firm's cash],
  [his capital, his current account balance and his share of goodwill],
  [his share of the next year's profit],
  [his capital only]
)

#mcq(10, [Goodwill on the retirement of a partner is credited to the retiring partner and debited to],
  [the continuing partners in their new ratio],
  [the realisation account],
  [the bank account],
  [the revaluation account]
)

#mcq(11, [If a retiring partner is not paid at once, his balance is transferred to],
  [the goodwill account],
  [a loan account],
  [the capital reserve],
  [the current account of the remaining partners]
)

#mcq(12, [On dissolution, the account that collects the proceeds of the assets is the],
  [appropriation account],
  [revaluation account],
  [current account],
  [realisation account]
)

#mcq(13, [In the realisation account, the assets are entered at],
  [their book value],
  [nil],
  [their selling price],
  [their replacement cost]
)

#mcq(14, [Liabilities on dissolution are],
  [transferred to capital],
  [put through the realisation account],
  [ignored],
  [paid directly, debited to the liability and credited to the bank]
)

#mcq(15, [The correct order of payment on dissolution is],
  [partners' loans, creditors, expenses, capital],
  [creditors, expenses, capital, loans],
  [expenses of realisation, outside creditors, partners' loans, partners' capital],
  [partners' capital, partners' loans, creditors, expenses]
)

#mcq(16, [A partner who has lent money to the firm is, for that loan,],
  [not entitled to repayment],
  [a creditor, paid before any capital],
  [a debtor of the firm],
  [an owner, paid last]
)

#mcq(17, [A partner's capital account shows a debit balance on dissolution. He must],
  [be paid that amount],
  [bring in cash to clear it],
  [transfer it to goodwill],
  [receive it from the bank]
)

#mcq(18, [A revaluation account is closed by transferring its balance to],
  [the realisation account],
  [the bank account],
  [the profit and loss account],
  [the partners' capital accounts]
)

#mcq(19, [On admission, if the new partner's capital is below his share of the total capital, the difference is],
  [paid into the bank],
  [ignored],
  [written off as goodwill],
  [debited to his current account and credited to the others]
)

#mcq(20, [X, Y and Z share profits equally. On Z's retirement the goodwill of ₦120,000 is to be adjusted in the books. Z's share is],
  [₦40,000],
  [₦30,000],
  [₦60,000],
  [₦120,000]
)

#mcq(21, [Using the last figures, X and Y continue in partnership and share profits and losses equally. Each bears],
  [₦20,000],
  [₦40,000],
  [₦60,000],
  [nil]
)

#mcq(22, [The revaluation account is prepared],
  [after the new partner is admitted],
  [only when a loss is expected],
  [before any change in the partnership],
  [only on dissolution]
)

#mcq(23, [Goodwill appears in the balance sheet of a partnership only when],
  [a partner retires],
  [the firm is dissolved],
  [it has been purchased for a consideration],
  [the partners agree to value it]
)

#mcq(24, [On dissolution, an asset with a book value of ₦50,000 is sold for ₦38,000. The realisation account shows],
  [a loss of ₦12,000],
  [a loss of ₦38,000],
  [no entry],
  [a profit of ₦12,000]
)

#mcq(25, [Expenses of realisation are],
  [ignored],
  [credited to the realisation account],
  [debited to the realisation account],
  [charged to the partners' current accounts directly]
)

#mcq(26, [A provision for doubtful debts released on dissolution is],
  [a debit in the realisation account],
  [a credit in the realisation account],
  [a liability],
  [a capital reserve]
)

#mcq(27, [The balance on the realisation account represents],
  [the cash available],
  [the profit or loss on the disposal of the firm's assets],
  [the partners' drawings],
  [the goodwill]
)

#mcq(28, [When a new partner is admitted, the old partners' capital accounts are credited with],
  [their share of the goodwill brought in],
  [the firm's profit],
  [the new partner's cash],
  [the whole of the revaluation]
)

#mcq(29, [A partnership deed may provide for all of the following EXCEPT],
  [a salary to a partner],
  [the profit-sharing ratio],
  [interest on capital],
  [the firm's income tax rate]
)

#mcq(30, [On the admission of a partner, if goodwill is not to remain in the books, the entry is to],
  [ignore goodwill altogether],
  [raise goodwill, then write it off among all partners],
  [debit the old partners and credit the new partner],
  [debit goodwill and credit the old partners]
)

#mcq(31, [A partner's current account is used to record],
  [interest on capital, salary, share of profit and drawings],
  [the capital he introduced],
  [the firm's bank balance],
  [the purchase of fixed assets]
)

#mcq(32, [If a partner takes goods from the firm for private use, the entry is],
  [no entry],
  [debit purchases, credit drawings],
  [debit drawings, credit purchases],
  [debit cash, credit sales]
)

#mcq(33, [On retirement, the revaluation profit is shared],
  [in the old ratio],
  [in the new ratio],
  [equally among the continuing partners],
  [by the retiring partner alone]
)

#mcq(34, [A firm is dissolved with assets of ₦500,000, outside liabilities ₦180,000 and a partner's loan of ₦60,000. After paying both, the cash left for capital is],
  [₦260,000],
  [₦320,000],
  [₦440,000],
  [₦200,000]
)

#mcq(35, [A new partner brings ₦80,000 cash for a one-fifth share. The goodwill implied by his payment, if the firm's net assets are ₦320,000, is],
  [₦16,000],
  [₦80,000],
  [nil],
  [₦320,000]
)

#mcq(36, [Which item is NOT debited to the realisation account?],
  [the expenses of realisation],
  [the book value of the assets],
  [a loss on the sale of an asset],
  [the proceeds of the assets sold]
)

#mcq(37, [A retiring partner's current account has a credit balance. It is],
  [ignored],
  [treated as a loan to the firm],
  [deducted from what he is owed],
  [added to what he is owed]
)

#mcq(38, [The main reason for revaluing assets on a change of partnership is to],
  [satisfy the tax authority],
  [increase the firm's profit],
  [ensure that no partner gains or loses from a change in the value of assets he did not create],
  [reduce the capital]
)

#mcq(39, [On dissolution, cash of ₦150,000 remains after all outside creditors and partners' loans are paid. The capitals are ₦90,000 and ₦60,000. The partners receive],
  [₦90,000 and ₦60,000],
  [₦150,000 to the first partner],
  [₦75,000 each],
  [nothing]
)

#mcq(40, [On admission, the balance on the revaluation account is transferred to the capital accounts],
  [in the new profit-sharing ratio],
  [equally],
  [of the new partner only],
  [in the old profit-sharing ratio]
)

